<section class="mx-auto max-w-readable px-5 py-12">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Terms of use</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
    Version <%= termsVersion %> · Last updated <%= updated %>
  </p>

  <div class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 p-4 text-red-900">
    <p class="font-bold">This is not a medical service.</p>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm">
      If you think you or your baby need help now, go to your nearest health facility.
      Do not wait for a reply here.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-slate-700">

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">1. What MamaTriage is</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        MamaTriage is a <strong>research prototype</strong> built for an MSc Information
        Technology project at MIVA Open University, Abuja. It asks about symptoms and
        suggests how urgently to seek care. It is being tested, and it can be wrong.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">2. What it is not</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li><strong>It is not a doctor</strong> and does not replace one.</li>
        <li><strong>It does not diagnose.</strong> It will never tell you what condition
            you or your baby have.</li>
        <li><strong>It does not prescribe.</strong> It will never tell you which medicine
            to take or how much.</li>
        <li><strong>It is not an emergency service.</strong> It cannot call an ambulance
            or alert anyone on your behalf.</li>
        <li><strong>It is not monitored.</strong> No person reads your messages as they
            arrive.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">3. Who it is for</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Mothers in the first year after giving birth, and infants from birth to
        12 months. If you ask about anyone else, it will tell you it cannot help and
        suggest you see a health worker.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        You must be 18 or older to register.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">4. What we ask of you</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li>Answer honestly. Wrong information leads to wrong advice.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Always seek care if you are worried</strong>, whatever the system says.
          Your judgement about your own baby matters more than a message on a phone.
        </li>
        <li>Do not use it in place of care a health worker has already advised.</li>
        <li>Do not send other people's personal details.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">5. Limits and errors</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        The system is designed to be cautious: when it is unsure, it tells you to get
        seen. Even so, it may be wrong in either direction — it may raise an alarm
        unnecessarily, or it may fail to recognise something serious.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        It may also be unavailable. If it cannot answer, it will send you a list of danger
        signs and tell you to go to a health facility if any apply.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">6. Taking part in the research</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        By registering you agree to take part in this study and to be contacted on the
        channel you chose. Your anonymised conversations will be used to evaluate whether
        the system is safe and accurate.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Taking part is voluntary. You may stop at any time by sending <strong>STOP</strong>,
        and you may ask for your data to be deleted. Neither will disadvantage you in any
        way.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">7. Cost</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        MamaTriage is free. Your network may charge you for data used to send and receive
        messages.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">8. Changes</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        If these terms change materially, we will ask you to agree again. The version you
        accepted is recorded with your registration.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>

  <p class="mt-10 text-center">
    <a href="/register" class="btn-primary">Back to registration</a>
  </p>
</section>
